From: vinegar-fork <local@localhost>
Date: Wed, 26 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/15] winex11: Restore ignoring WM config changes in
 virtual desktop mode

Patch 0008 in this patchset reverts an upstream commit wholesale to
fix invisible QT menus, which also removed the guard that makes Wine
ignore window-manager-driven resize/configure events while running in
virtual desktop mode. Without that guard, some Wayland compositors
(observed on KDE Plasma / KWin) end up resizing the virtual desktop's
top-level window to fill the entire output, overriding the
configured Desktop resolution and causing the compositor to treat it
as if it were fullscreen (hiding panels/taskbars, no visible
decorations).

This re-adds just that guard on top of 0008, without reverting the
rest of it (StructureNotifyMask stays removed, the
configure_serial-on-Withdraw fix stays), as a targeted experiment.

Signed-off-by: vinegar-fork <local@localhost>
---
 dlls/winex11.drv/window.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c b/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
index ebeabdcc465..1a2b3c4d5e6 100644
--- a/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winex11.drv/window.c
@@ -1745,6 +1745,7 @@ static UINT window_update_client_config( struct x11drv_win_data *data )
     UINT flags;
 
     if (!data->managed) return 0; /* unmanaged windows are managed by the Win32 side */
+    if (is_virtual_desktop()) return 0; /* ignore window manager config changes in virtual desktop mode */
     if (data->desired_state.wm_state != NormalState) return 0; /* ignore config changes on invisible/minimized windows */
 
     if (data->wm_state_serial) return 0; /* another WM_STATE update is pending, wait for it to complete */
